[[Open This|3. Rack network management]]

---

Integrating an Oxide rack into the on-premises network involves the allocation of IP addresses and configuration of rack switches. There are five basic elements on a rack switch that may be configured:

# Ports carry physical layer (L1).
# Links carry link layer (L2) information.
# Interfaces carry internet layer (L3) information and typically belong to a port.
# Addresses are assigned to interfaces.
# Routes determine forwarding behavior across the switch.